# Config file reference

<!-- Generated by scripts/gen_config_docs.py from src/wot_toolchain/schemas/config.yaml. Edit the schema, not this page. -->

A project describes what to generate in a YAML config file, by default `wot-toolchain.yaml` in the current directory (select another with `-c`).
Relative paths in the file are resolved against the directory of the config file.

## The config file and its schema

Two files are involved, and they play different roles:

| File | Owned by | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `wot-toolchain.yaml` | The project that uses the toolchain | The **config file**: an instance that says which LinkML schemas to read, which generators to run and where their output goes. This repository has one for the Thing Description; another repository brings its own. |
| `src/wot_toolchain/schemas/config.yaml` | The toolchain, shipped inside the package | The **config schema**: a LinkML schema that defines which keys a config file may have, their types and which are required. It describes the format, not any project. |

The config schema is to a config file what a JSON Schema is to a JSON document.
Do not confuse it with the vocabulary schemas in `resources/schemas/`, which describe the Thing Description and are what the generators turn into artifacts; the config schema is never generated from.

When the toolchain starts, `config.py` reads the config file and validates it against the config schema with the LinkML validator, so a missing key, a wrong type or an unknown key fails with an `ERROR` naming the file and the location.
It then makes the checks a schema cannot express: input paths must exist, prefixes and vocabulary schemas must be unique, `jsonschema` and `spec` need settings, and a section or snippet schema must refer to a listed vocabulary or generator.

This page is generated from the config schema by `scripts/gen_config_docs.py`, so it lists exactly the keys the validator accepts.
To add or change a key, change the config schema (and `config.py`, which reads the value), then regenerate this page; do not edit the page itself.

The top level of a config file is [`{{ schemaview.tree_root.name if schemaview.tree_root else "Config" }}`](#config). The repository's own [`wot-toolchain.yaml`](https://github.com/w3c/wot-thing-description-toolchain-tmp/blob/main/wot-toolchain.yaml) is a complete example.

